From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:10:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk/csf: re-emit the VS FAU and SRT registers after an
 indirect draw

launch_indirect_draw() runs one RUN_IDVS per indirect draw in a CS loop.
When the VS reads first_vertex or base_instance, each iteration patches them
into its own copy of the VS push uniforms and then adds one copy's size to
VERTEX_FAU; with repeated vertex descriptors it does the same to VERTEX_SRT.
After the loop both registers point one copy past the end, and the copies
hold the GPU-patched values of the indirect draws.

The next draw rewrote them only if its own dirty state said so. A direct
draw that follows with the same first vertex and base instance (so no
sysval changed) and no vertex input change read its push uniforms and, with
repeated descriptors, its resource table from past the end of those
allocations. Nothing hid it except an unrelated rebuild: until now a
rebuilt FS driver set flagged DESC_STATE, which rewrote VERTEX_SRT too.

Flag VS_PUSH_UNIFORMS after every indirect draw, and VB after one with
repeated descriptors, so the next draw uploads fresh push uniforms and
rebuilds the VS tables, writing both registers. This only adds work after
indirect draws. Found while removing that DESC_STATE side effect (next
commit); upstream Mesa has the same loop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAYrqSPd4TgpVaKLqz5cYR

Purpose: fix B14: after an indirect draw the CS loop leaves VERTEX_FAU (and VERTEX_SRT with repeated descriptors) one copy past the end, so a following direct draw with nothing dirty read push uniforms past the allocation; flag VS_PUSH_UNIFORMS (and VB) after indirect draws so the next draw rewrites them. Upstream Mesa has the same loop; only adds work after indirect draws, no switch
Upstream-commit: none
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: none (fix of upstream code); required by rg477m/027, which removes the FS rebuild that used to rewrite VERTEX_SRT by accident; applies on the full g615-v11-csf series after rg477m/025
Validation test: part of the device-tested draw-path batch rg477m/023-027: PanProbe 38/38 x2; Arkham Asylum (CPU-bound DXVK, quietd Stock, 10 interleaved rounds + 3) gameplay fps unchanged (median 36.4 base vs 36.55), launch failures 0/13 base vs 2/13 (known B5 signatures, Fisher p~0.48, n.s.); not tested on its own (dEQP draw.*indirect* / shader_draw_parameters not run); no game known to mix indirect and direct draws (vkd3d-proton) checked separately; combined build next.so (15c3385bbe40, rg477m/023-037): PanProbe 38/38 x2 (unsafe profile 37/38, only the bc_decode raw readback, by design); 16-game boot sweep 2026-10-25 in quietd Stock mode: Hades 60, Jupiter Hell 59, Risk of Rain 2 38, Moonlighter 60, Megabonk 60, Portal 2 60, Gladius 60, Crysis 3 Remastered 60 fps; Arkham Asylum to the menu; Factorio and Ashes menus render as before; Descenders, Tomb Raider, Doom 3 BFG and Metro 2033 match their known states; 0 GPU faults; Serious Sam bot benchmark A-B-B-A compat 49.2/52.7 vs next 53.3/51.1 fps; Arkham Asylum 20-round interleaved A/B 2026-10-25 (quietd Stock), base rg477m vs next: launch failures 1/20 vs 0/20 (session total 1/33 vs 4/36, not significant; B5 signatures also seen on the stock driver), gameplay fps median 36.4 vs 36.5, speckcount on 3 gameplay frames per run 0-1 px in both arms (base 2 runs with 1 px, next 3 runs with 1 px; the old specks bug gave tens to hundreds): no specks
Channel: compatibility, unsafe
